1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,154
PACT. The payment authorization gateway for AI agents.

2
00:00:04,154 --> 00:00:08,407
Let any agent shop for you, only within the limits you set.

3
00:00:09,133 --> 00:00:11,071
AI agents can now shop for us.

4
00:00:11,071 --> 00:00:13,876
But to pay, we hand them a card with no limits.

5
00:00:13,876 --> 00:00:15,304
One injected prompt,

6
00:00:15,304 --> 00:00:18,359
and real money moves before anyone approves it.

7
00:00:18,817 --> 00:00:21,910
PACT sits between any AI agent and PayPal.

8
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:23,643
Agents can only ask.

9
00:00:23,643 --> 00:00:26,674
A deterministic policy engine authorizes,

10
00:00:26,674 --> 00:00:29,771
a human approves, and PayPal executes.

11
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:32,046
Set your rules once.

12
00:00:32,046 --> 00:00:37,511
This mandate allows desk tech from five retailers, at most $150 an item.

13
00:00:37,511 --> 00:00:41,587
Anything up to $100 is authorized automatically.

14
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:43,936
An agent asks for a mouse.

15
00:00:43,936 --> 00:00:48,259
Channel3 searches real retailers, Gemini picks the cheapest offer,

16
00:00:48,259 --> 00:00:51,939
and every rule passes, so PACT authorizes it by itself.

17
00:00:51,939 --> 00:00:53,708
No approval click.

18
00:00:54,067 --> 00:00:56,623
PACT creates a real PayPal Sandbox order,

19
00:00:56,623 --> 00:00:59,637
and the buyer approves it in PayPal Checkout.

20
00:00:59,983 --> 00:01:03,542
The moment PayPal confirms, PACT captures automatically:

21
00:01:03,542 --> 00:01:07,267
a real Sandbox capture ID, completed, for the exact amount.

22
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:10,602
This is Sandbox money, so no Newegg order is placed.

23
00:01:10,602 --> 00:01:14,355
PACT only hands the buyer off to Newegg's own checkout.

24
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:17,242
A $109.99 keyboard passes every rule too,

25
00:01:17,242 --> 00:01:19,265
but it is above the auto limit.

26
00:01:19,265 --> 00:01:20,873
So PACT stops and asks,

27
00:01:20,873 --> 00:01:23,873
and my approval is sealed with a fingerprint.

28
00:01:24,216 --> 00:01:27,547
A SHA-256 hash of the product, merchant, price,

29
00:01:27,547 --> 00:01:30,758
quantity, mandate rules and requesting agent.

30
00:01:30,758 --> 00:01:32,999
A forged approval is refused,

31
00:01:32,999 --> 00:01:37,065
and the hash is checked again before every PayPal step.

32
00:01:37,399 --> 00:01:39,712
And this offer is blocked outright:

33
00:01:39,712 --> 00:01:43,530
a retailer I never allowed, over the item cap, and over budget.

34
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:46,469
There is no approve button to override it.

35
00:01:46,816 --> 00:01:49,558
Connecting an outside agent takes seconds.

36
00:01:49,558 --> 00:01:51,970
It gets one mandate and its own key,

37
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:54,687
shown once and stored only as a hash.

38
00:01:55,033 --> 00:01:57,904
Any agent can call PACT through its REST API

39
00:01:57,904 --> 00:02:01,383
or its MCP server. This Gemini agent connects over MCP,

40
00:02:01,383 --> 00:02:03,316
is told money is no object,

41
00:02:03,316 --> 00:02:05,112
and still gets a no.

42
00:02:06,716 --> 00:02:09,768
Every decision is audited and charted with AG Studio.

43
00:02:09,768 --> 00:02:12,320
Its own AI agents can analyze the spending,

44
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:14,672
but they can never approve or pay.

45
00:02:15,033 --> 00:02:18,554
Any platform plugs in with one connector that returns offers.

46
00:02:18,554 --> 00:02:20,697
The policy engine, the fingerprint

47
00:02:20,697 --> 00:02:23,039
and the PayPal flow never change.

48
00:02:23,516 --> 00:02:26,962
Agents request. The policy engine authorizes.

49
00:02:26,962 --> 00:02:29,692
A human approves. PayPal executes.

50
00:02:29,692 --> 00:02:33,973
PACT. The payment authorization gateway for AI agents.
